                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7afd11b0-6b52-37c5-b6f9-eca9ed1d0510",
                                        "entry_id": "08102bf3-433e-33b9-8819-6d936484c19b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In screw theory, a screw assembled from force and torque vectors arising from application of Newton's laws to a rigid body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c7c0762-0241-313d-b8f7-792b72564764",
                                        "entry_id": "08102bf3-433e-33b9-8819-6d936484c19b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "means; contrivance"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c4313c-86f7-4998-9163-161894732edc",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7c0762-0241-313d-b8f7-792b72564764",
                                                "text": "But weighing one thing with another he gave Britain for lost; but resolved to make his profit of this business of Britain, as a quarrel for war; and that of Naples, as a wrench and mean for peace"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c957cbc-c6c3-3f9e-af98-d97ab6494106",
                                        "entry_id": "08102bf3-433e-33b9-8819-6d936484c19b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In coursing, the act of bringing the hare round at less than a right angle, worth half a point in the recognised code of points for judging."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wrench",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e44a04c-564e-376f-8729-dc6b8157b37c",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pull or twist violently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "756ef46e-4a75-4d16-8689-4acaab7e6c7f",
                                                "sense_id": "5e44a04c-564e-376f-8729-dc6b8157b37c",
                                                "text": "With a surge of adrenaline, she wrenched the car door off and pulled out the injured man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41ce3972-bf51-398f-9b3c-77a815c0e27e",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To injure (a joint) by pulling or twisting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b02fefd-46d7-44b8-bf16-2ef423148fce",
                                                "sense_id": "41ce3972-bf51-398f-9b3c-77a815c0e27e",
                                                "text": "Be careful not to wrench your ankle walking along those loose stones!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c187a06-be4d-3a82-bb01-80639d2ffb39",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To distort the original meaning of; to misrepresent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "680e3168-ca0a-3b79-a5ee-6123022e75e0",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rack with pain; to make hurt or distressed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a295ba7f-3773-4103-9b92-1201ab082274",
                                                "sense_id": "680e3168-ca0a-3b79-a5ee-6123022e75e0",
                                                "text": "And what actinic, mind-wrenching form could the countermeme take? How could human hands assemble something so devastatingly powerful and hold it steady; what human mind could wield it without exploding from the inside out?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9125a20e-fb4c-3fc6-842c-9eebea4a2804",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deprive by means of a violent pull or twist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53c8ce73-f399-3726-94c6-998e3f292b3a",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use a wrench; to twist with a wrench."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e23ec31f-00d2-45e1-abc8-7a3289fba7fb",
                                                "sense_id": "53c8ce73-f399-3726-94c6-998e3f292b3a",
                                                "text": "The plumber wrenched the pipes until they came loose."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b563c26d-45a0-3949-8f4e-e7f8c151e8c1",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To violently move in a turn or writhe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72a7f6e8-24be-33ba-a61d-2644c59d656f",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tighten with or as if with a winch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c695f016-ea2e-434a-b073-7a2b477552e5",
                                                "sense_id": "72a7f6e8-24be-33ba-a61d-2644c59d656f",
                                                "text": "[S]end me that hag hither; she shall avouch what it was that she hath given to the wretch Dryfesdale, or the pilniewinks and thumbikins shall wrench it out of her finger-joints."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f3524d7-7956-3569-b8c0-71882b8faeb2",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To thrust (a weapon) in a twisting motion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77308fb4-10b3-36df-a5cf-c953e94033a9",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disarm an opponent by whirling their blade away."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "414370d7-c339-474c-a0d3-3dba0d021fbb",
                        "source_entry_id": "b89baee1-42a5-3c76-8313-40c140fe08ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "419648c8-80a6-3e90-8ece-49594a08706d",
                        "target_lang_word": "lever",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lever",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c1191bf-8054-309e-974c-bfce98a6866f",
                                        "entry_id": "3638a07e-fc64-3ef6-a688-59b65e6a772b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rigid piece which is capable of turning about one point, or axis (fulcrum), and in which are two or more other points where forces are applied; — used for transmitting and modifying force and motion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8caa381c-0661-3725-8bdf-3505cd70905e",
                                        "entry_id": "3638a07e-fc64-3ef6-a688-59b65e6a772b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rigid piece which is capable of turning about one point, or axis (fulcrum), and in which are two or more other points where forces are applied; — used for transmitting and modifying force and motion.",
                                            "Specifically, a bar of metal, wood or other rigid substance, used to exert a pressure, or sustain a weight, at one point of its length, by receiving a force or power at a second, and turning at a third on a fixed point called a fulcrum. It is usually named as the first of the six mechanical powers, and is of three kinds, according as either the fulcrum F, the weight W, or the power P, respectively, is situated between the other two, as in the figures."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b213a82-0b42-477e-a6a9-2912a3d831c0",
                                                "sense_id": "8caa381c-0661-3725-8bdf-3505cd70905e",
                                                "text": "Retractable steps and handrails are provided on each side of the cars. The steps, which are under the control of the guard, are operated by hand levers in the entrance vestibule."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2ce723c-67e5-3c66-bd5c-a94cdfdd1c00",
                                        "entry_id": "3638a07e-fc64-3ef6-a688-59b65e6a772b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small such piece to trigger or control a mechanical device (like a switch or a button)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4337f5fb-c38c-3c44-90ed-ac65de2ebacc",
                                        "entry_id": "3638a07e-fc64-3ef6-a688-59b65e6a772b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bar, as a capstan bar, applied to a rotatory piece to turn it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e48ac7bd-2d2f-43d1-ab47-3dcb61a159bf",
                                                "sense_id": "4337f5fb-c38c-3c44-90ed-ac65de2ebacc",
                                                "text": "A doorknob of whatever roundish shape is effectively a continuum of levers, with the axis of the latching mechanism—known as the spindle—being the fulcrum about which the turning takes place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f25b9788-b518-3eea-908e-32159fd4c41b",
                                        "entry_id": "3638a07e-fc64-3ef6-a688-59b65e6a772b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An arm on a rock shaft, to give motion to the shaft or to obtain motion from it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de5cf01f-bde6-37d9-9fd2-9e8ca502562e",
                                        "entry_id": "3638a07e-fc64-3ef6-a688-59b65e6a772b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crowbar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ecf7e8d-077a-43fa-ba5c-a7b6a7aec60a",
                                                "sense_id": "de5cf01f-bde6-37d9-9fd2-9e8ca502562e",
                                                "text": "My lord, I brained him with a lever my neighbour lent me, and he stood by and cried, ‘Strike home, old boy!’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lever",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "890ce97d-24ec-34c8-bc1f-cb8f54301c9a",
                                        "entry_id": "fa83f755-0ae8-3343-8632-ba42907958d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move with a lever."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c4d6f7e-6ec8-45de-aa2f-d9f1597d72d1",
                                                "sense_id": "890ce97d-24ec-34c8-bc1f-cb8f54301c9a",
                                                "text": "With great effort and a big crowbar I managed to lever the beam off the floor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3e27753-0c09-4472-a41a-8a80652db805",
                                                "sense_id": "890ce97d-24ec-34c8-bc1f-cb8f54301c9a",
                                                "text": "Someone found a pick and levered a burst plank out of the floor, and in a few minutes we had got a fire alight and our drenched clothes were steaming."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b621c96-6ff4-35bd-a248-3e226b24018b",
                                        "entry_id": "fa83f755-0ae8-3343-8632-ba42907958d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use, operate or move (something) like a lever (physically)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07f4e695-74be-4300-bbc2-7566bfedf040",
                                                "sense_id": "4b621c96-6ff4-35bd-a248-3e226b24018b",
                                                "text": "Sullen now, with stultified spleen, Mrs Dibble grappled her crutches and levered herself upright after an ungainly struggle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f58653d-4c80-4495-bd8d-c03c51ba6d80",
                                                "sense_id": "4b621c96-6ff4-35bd-a248-3e226b24018b",
                                                "text": "Suddenly he had levered himself up from the sofa, rocking the lame man violently, and was walking towards the receptionist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7517e913-2f91-445d-9ca5-5a900bfe5f48",
                                                "sense_id": "4b621c96-6ff4-35bd-a248-3e226b24018b",
                                                "text": "The guard at the door coughed up blood, and died instantly. Fina was carrying an empty rifle with a sharpened bayonet, and she'd thrust it straight up through his neck, severing the spinal cord. She levered him off the front stoop and into the bushes, then stood up on the tips of her toes to peer through the window in the door."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfdfa5ef-897f-33f1-974e-bb1af8ca845d",
                                        "entry_id": "fa83f755-0ae8-3343-8632-ba42907958d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use (something) like a lever (in an abstract sense)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23f3dd97-6fc9-47a5-8497-a039becbc364",
                                                "sense_id": "bfdfa5ef-897f-33f1-974e-bb1af8ca845d",
                                                "text": "He was a man who levered his way from small-time communist hack to political power by tapping into the most potent vein of historical juice in the Balkans: nationalism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ef583dd-ec86-46f2-8ffc-da49745844da",
                                                "sense_id": "bfdfa5ef-897f-33f1-974e-bb1af8ca845d",
                                                "text": "Credited with pioneering the detective novel, Collins has attracted many biographers over the years, drawn to his extraordinary life and work in the hope of levering open a new understanding of the Victorian psyche."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1cb0e781-c02f-3cea-a0b8-98293723da27",
                                        "entry_id": "fa83f755-0ae8-3343-8632-ba42907958d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To increase the share of debt in the capitalization of a business."
